// # oodar — Gen 1 Host Substrate (v2.1.0)
//
// Logline: The canonical home of the openOODA Gen 1 host substrate. Compiled openOODA binaries link against the oo_* symbols exported from the 6 per-domain subdirs; the build entry point is `gcc oodar.c`.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The 6 per-domain tactical subdirs mirror std's vocabulary (core, sec, fs, net, hw, app). Each tactical subdir has its own ANCHOR.oo. Some tactical subdirs have nested sub-subdirs (e.g., core/str/, sec/cap/, app/actor/) that also have their own ANCHOR.oo, mirroring std's per-domain organization. The umbrella oodar.c is the single-TU build entry — it #include's the 48 .c files in dependency order. The public API is oodar.h (and the shared type defs in types.h) at the root. The qa/ subdir now holds the 2 test utilities (oo_hip_so_smoke.c, dudect_c_native.c); they are excluded from the umbrella TU and are not part of the public ABI.
//
// Beats (read in this order):
//   1. types.h          — shared type defs (OoStr, OoIList, OoRes*, OoLL*, OoControlBlock, OoWeakRef, ...).
//   2. oodar.h          — the public API surface.
//   3. oodar.c          — the umbrella TU (the canonical single-TU build entry).
//   4. core/            — mirrors std/core. Universal primitives: str, list, mem, math, meta.
//   5. sec/             — mirrors std/sec. Security primitives: cap (25 tokens: 14 NORTHSTAR core + 11 future-state), landlock (Pillar 9), crypto, pqc (PQC-by-default).
//   6. fs/              — mirrors std/fs. Filesystem + host OS: os (syscalls, DNS loopback, rlimit), io (print).
//   7. net/             — mirrors std/net. Network primitives: fetch, tls.
//   8. hw/              — mirrors std/hw. Hardware: gpu (HIP/ROCm, no CPU fallback).
//   9. app/             — mirrors std/app. Application bridges: actor (OTP-style concurrency), xlang (FFI), hitl (TTY), telemetry (metrics + event bus).
//  10. qa/              — test utilities (oo_hip_so_smoke.c, dudect_c_native.c); not part of the ABI.
//  11. scripts/, docs/, examples/ — scaffolding (unchanged from v1.0.0).
//
// Naming convention:
//   - Files: <tactical>/<sub>.c  (no file prefix; one concept per file)
//   - Headers: oodar.h + types.h at root, per-subdir <thing>.h
//   - Symbols: oo_* (the openOODA namespace; language-agnostic, project-namespaced)
//   - Tactical subdirs each have an ANCHOR.oo
//   - Sub-subdirs (e.g., core/str/, sec/cap/, app/actor/) each have an ANCHOR.oo
//
// Build:
//   gcc oodar.c                           (the canonical single-TU build)
//   gcc -c <tactical>/<sub>/<file>.c      (per-file compile, link all .o)
//
// Versioning:
//   v2.1.0 is a Patch bump from v2.0.0. No ABI change (function signatures
//   are unchanged). Security-hardening: reversed the inverted bounds check
//   in oo_write_int/oo_read_int (was: foreign pointer with bad magic
//   silently bypassed the bound check, giving an AllocCap holder arbitrary
//   R/W); added Landlock-APPLIED gate to oo_proc_mem_read (was: only
//   checked Landlock AVAILABLE, so any caller could read /proc/self/mem
//   without ever calling oo_sandbox_apply); fixed silent rejection-
//   sampling bug in mldsa.c (was: `while (ctr<256) { ...; break; }` left
//   coefficients uninitialised); fixed arena_alloc overflow on
//   `a->off + n > a->cap`; removed 5 dead cap tokens (AUDIT, HITL, SYNC,
//   MEM, HTTP) and the 3 dead event subscriptions (cap.seal, fs.read,
//   fs.write); removed declared-but-not-implemented fs_file_size; moved
//   test utilities (oo_hip_so_smoke, dudect_c_native) from production
//   tree to qa/; corrected the cap-rpc cap from ThreadCap to SignCap
//   (sign-style operation, not thread-style). See CHANGES.md for the
//   full list of what changed, what did not, and what the next Floor
//   break (v3.0.0) will cover.
//   Per RULES.oot §1.24 + RFC-0006, every push to main triggers an
//   auto-release via the governance workflow.
//
// ──▓▓ oodar ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: api_surface = 52 :: VERSION = 2.1.0 :: Pillar 3 + Pillar 5 + Pillar 7 + Pillar 9 ::
